1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,240
This series was created
for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:05,680
The characters, actions, locations,
dialogue, languages, ceremonies,

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,120
and artistic elements depicted in this series

4
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,040
are fictional and based on imagination,

5
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:13,920
incorporating the beauty
of the region's diverse cultures,

6
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:18,400
including those
of Lanna, Myanmar, the Tai peoples, and China.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,560
It is not intended to disrespect any history,

8
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,600
ethnic group, organization, profession,
or group of individuals.

9
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,040
Viewer discretion is advised.

10
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,520
[Previously]
<i>Thank you so much, Mr. Bew,</i>

11
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:29,800
<i>for teaching me
the physical therapy exercises.</i>

12
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:30,520
<i>Bew!</i>

13
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:31,640
<i>Do you know him?</i>

14
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:35,160
<i>And thank you
for giving me a reason to live again.</i>

15
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,200
<i>What is your name, then?</i>

16
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,000
<i>I could sing for you instead.</i>

17
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:38,920
<i>Just look at you.</i>

18
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:40,520
<i>I doubt you could even find
your way back to your residence.</i>

19
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,360
<i>Once I ascend the throne,</i>

20
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:45,240
<i>everything in this palace will belong to me.</i>

21
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:47,600
<i>How can our marriage ever work</i>

22
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,120
<i>when the man
who is supposed to be her life partner</i>

23
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:51,840
<i>can't make her happy?</i>

24
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:56,960
<i>The actor auditioning for Phaya Devaraja
was in an accident?</i>

25
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,080
<i>Yeah.</i>

26
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:02,120
<i>Isn't that the third accident
since we started casting?</i>

27
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:03,960
<i>Yes.</i>

28
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,800
<i>Guys, I don't think
these are coincidences anymore.</i>

29
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,120
<i>- Maybe this king is bringing us bad luck.
- You're right.</i>

30
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:14,040
<i>Should we change the lead character, Boon?</i>

31
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:16,560
<i>Or maybe consult a fortune teller.</i>

32
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:20,280
<i>They could help us decide whose story to tell.</i>

33
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:27,000
<i>But Phaya Devaraja is
the most complex character.</i>

34
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,200
<i>If we tell the story through someone else,
we'll lose some of the storylines.</i>

35
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,120
<i>And we'd stray from the main theme.</i>

36
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:37,760
<i>Can we please stick with him for now?</i>

37
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:42,640
<i>The accidents were probably just coincidences.</i>

38
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,360
<i>I'm sure...</i>

39
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:52,640
<i>we'll find the right actor soon.</i>

40
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,120
<i>Let's keep him as the lead.</i>

41
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,600
<i>Okay.</i>

42
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:06,920
<i>We'll try contacting another actor.</i>

43
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:10,000
<i>But this is the last actor we'll try.</i>

44
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:14,520
<i>If anything else goes wrong,
I'll have to change the storyline.</i>

45
00:03:54,520 --> 00:04:01,960
[Forbidden City]

46
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:12,160
- These are fresh. I'll take a bunch.
- Would you like some more today?

47
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:14,840
Would you like the ones
you ordered before as well?

48
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,880
The ones you ordered last time?

49
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:21,200
These two have just come in.
I only got them this morning.

50
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,000
This smells lovely.

51
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,280
Yes.

52
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:37,240
- We'll take these two as well.
- These two as well?

53
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:39,600
- Yes.
- Of course.

54
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:42,360
<i>I barely got to enjoy my fabulous new life.</i>

55
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:44,480
Now I'm back to slaving away.

56
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:49,080
It's just cooking. How hard can it be?

57
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:54,640
Lha, I'll take care of dinner.

58
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,320
What would you like to eat?

59
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,520
Are you all right?

60
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:11,160
- Are you all right?
- It hurts.

61
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:12,280
Be still.

62
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,160
Careful.

63
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,880
Can you walk?

64
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,960
Please sit down.

65
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:26,520
Please sit down. Let me take a look.

66
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:28,680
What are you doing?

67
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:32,560
Earlier, you had a sharp pain
that stopped you from getting up.

68
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:37,520
But have you felt any pain or numbness
radiating from your hips down your legs?

69
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:44,000
When you change positions,
whether standing, walking, or sitting,

70
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,280
do you feel tightness around here as well?

71
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,480
Just as I thought.

72
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,320
Please lie down. Lha.

73
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,320
- My lady?
- Help me.

74
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,520
- What on earth are you doing?
- Please lie down.

75
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,920
Please raise your legs slowly.

76
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:07,360
Lady Fongnuan?

77
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:12,480
I'll massage your muscles to help them relax.

78
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:15,320
It might hurt a little,
but you'll feel better afterward.

79
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:17,840
<i>The piriformis muscle is right here.</i>

80
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,720
This might hurt a little.

81
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:39,320
<i>This is called piriformis syndrome.</i>

82
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:41,720
<i>It happens
when the piriformis muscle compresses a nerve.</i>

83
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:42,760
<i>It usually occurs</i>

84
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:45,160
<i>when someone stays in the same position
for too long,</i>

85
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:48,000
<i>whether sitting, standing, or lying down
for extended periods,</i>

86
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
<i>like your mother.</i>

87
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,080
Are you feeling better?

88
00:06:56,240 --> 00:07:00,320
From now on, please avoid standing or sitting
in one position for too long.

89
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:03,800
It's best to keep moving
to improve your circulation.

90
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:08,160
If possible, try applying warm compresses

91
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:12,720
and doing daily exercises
to stretch these muscles.

92
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:18,800
Otherwise, you may eventually
lose the ability to walk.

93
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,720
Try stretching your legs.

94
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,600
Does that feel better?

95
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:44,080
Well, are you a masseuse or a fortune teller?

96
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:47,960
You talk as if you can see my future.

97
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:53,320
How do you know I spend so much time
sitting or standing in one position?

98
00:07:55,680 --> 00:08:00,320
I've known someone who had symptoms like yours.

99
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:06,400
Thank you very much.

100
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,800
Where are you from?

101
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,320
What is your name?

102
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:16,160
My name is Fongnuan. I'm from Wang Nam Lin.

103
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:21,000
Lady Fongnuan is Princess Maneethip's cousin.

104
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,240
She's currently staying
at Wiang Kaew's House of Guests.

105
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:29,200
And how do you know all this?

106
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,840
I've been wondering that myself.

107
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:37,080
How do you know, my lady?

108
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:40,080
I've served you since you were little.

109
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:42,400
You never knew any of this before.

110
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:44,560
Well...

111
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,080
It happened that day.

112
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:49,160
When I woke up during the ceremony,

113
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:53,480
it felt like a sign from above.

114
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:56,640
What ceremony?

115
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:02,000
The Water Spirit Ceremony.

116
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,720
Lady Fongnuan lost consciousness.

117
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:07,440
When she came to,

118
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:11,400
she might have had a vision.

119
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:15,120
That's right. Exactly what she said.

120
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,880
Thank you very much.

121
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:24,800
You're kind to a stranger.

122
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:29,560
Though you seem rather
eccentric, you came to my aid.

123
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:32,240
Perhaps there's more to you than your madness.

124
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:38,280
By the way, who did you come here with?

125
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:40,840
Would you like Lha and me
to escort you back to your residence?

126
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,800
There's no need.

127
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,400
My residence isn't far from here.
I can make my own way back.

128
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:48,560
Please be careful.

129
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,280
Have a safe journey home.

130
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:45,520
[Lady Homjan]

131
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:47,240
Lady Homjan.

132
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,960
Why have you summoned me?

133
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:59,800
Today, I met a young lady at the market.

134
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:03,400
She's quick on her feet, clever,

135
00:11:04,280 --> 00:11:07,720
and has a way with words.

136
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:10,280
I took quite a liking to her.

137
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,320
According to your books,

138
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:17,920
is today an unlucky day for me?

139
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:29,840
Today is an auspicious day.

140
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:34,000
Whatever comes your way today...

141
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,800
is sure to bring good fortune.

142
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:29,280
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.
- I pay my respects to you, Your Majesty.

143
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:27,120
The pedestal tray is ready, Your Majesty.

144
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:48,240
Please have some tea leaf wraps.

145
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:51,600
I've added salt, rock sugar, and sliced ginger,
just the way you like it.

146
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:55,560
But this time, I fermented the leaves
for a shorter time

147
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:58,120
to give them a more astringent taste.

148
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:02,280
Young people prefer their tea leaves sour.

149
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:06,880
But older folk like me
prefer a more astringent taste.

150
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:11,680
Are you suggesting that I'm old?

151
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:15,080
I'm getting older by the day myself.

152
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:19,120
Perhaps it's time I found someone else
to help care for you, Your Majesty.

153
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:22,200
You're still in good health.

154
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:24,320
You won't die before me.

155
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:27,520
Life is uncertain, Your Majesty.

156
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:31,520
If you should die, I shall follow you.

157
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:34,840
Please don't say that, Your Majesty.

158
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:41,560
I'm fortunate to have been blessed
with Your Majesty's kindness.

159
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,960
It is my duty...

160
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:47,520
to care for Your Majesty
to the best of my ability.

161
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:50,920
As for me,

162
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:55,800
if I can serve Your Majesty
until my dying breath,

163
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,720
I shall die in peace.

164
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:06,880
If Your Majesty would be so gracious,

165
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:09,840
I have a request to make.

166
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:12,320
Speak.

167
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:15,840
I met a young lady at the market today.

168
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:19,440
There was something special about her.

169
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:23,040
I believe she could be of great help
to Wiang Kaew.

170
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:29,720
You've never once asked me
to bring anyone into Wiang Kaew.

171
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:34,760
This young lady must be quite extraordinary.

172
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:44,920
- Cheers!
- Shia!

173
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:53,520
Is it wrong to be born a prince?

174
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:58,360
Why must social status
stand in the way of love?

175
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:02,400
Why must there be conditions?
Isn't love enough?

176
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:05,040
That's life.

177
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:09,280
Princes like you have it especially hard.

178
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:12,520
You were born into a life of comfort,

179
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:16,360
yet you can't find happiness
when it comes to love.

180
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,920
But don't despair.

181
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:24,240
You're not the only one
who struggles with love.

182
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:29,400
Even a normal lady like me
has the same troubles.

183
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:36,520
Being loved...

184
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:48,680
doesn't necessarily mean...

185
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:53,320
you'll be happy.

186
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:57,640
So that means,

187
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:00,760
regardless of our station in life,

188
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:04,480
we all suffer because of love.

189
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,840
You speak the truth, Senior.

190
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,920
Even so,

191
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:17,080
I still want to experience love.

192
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:21,840
<i>A woman.</i>

193
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:23,320
<i>Beautiful.</i>

194
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:29,200
<i>Unless you want to get hurt,
keep that shrill voice down.</i>

195
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,800
<i>You startled the horse.</i>

196
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:35,160
<i>What is your name, then?</i>

197
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:38,000
<i>I could sing for you instead.</i>

198
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,080
<i>Just look at you.</i>

199
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:41,240
<i>I doubt you could even find
your way back to your residence.</i>

200
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,080
<i>Wait!</i>

201
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:54,000
Are you in love, Kong Tai?

202
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:57,160
Are you in love, Kong Tai?

203
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,520
He's definitely smitten.

204
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:04,080
- Smitten?
- Smitten?

205
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:09,240
He's fallen in love.

206
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:19,120
Well, anyone can fall in love at first sight.

207
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:23,280
It's fate. It's destiny.

208
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:31,320
If fate has decreed that I must suffer,

209
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:33,040
I'd rather have none of it.

210
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:37,160
If I'm to be forced
to live with someone I don't love,

211
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:41,280
I'd rather never love at all.

212
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:43,280
I'd rather die!

213
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:47,280
If your heart can't take it,
don't go looking for love.

214
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:48,960
You'll only get hurt.

215
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:50,000
Cheers!

216
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,120
- Hey!
- Shia!

217
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:56,760
Did you all invite me out for drinks
just to make me listen to your sad stories?

218
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:58,360
Who's sad, Your Highness?

219
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:04,680
- I'm not sad.
- I'm... not sad either.

220
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,080
I'm sad.

221
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:17,760
I'd better get going.

222
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:20,760
I don't want to be around sad people.

223
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:24,160
If you want to be sad, suit yourselves.

224
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:27,200
Off you go, Fongnuan.

225
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:31,040
Goodbye, Fongnuan. Love is a wonderful thing.

226
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:34,080
- Don't be sad.
- I'm not sad, Your Highness.

227
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:36,600
Goodbye.

228
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:40,600
Who's sad? Nobody's sad!

229
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:42,320
- You're sad!
- Hello?

230
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,960
Bangkok, is that you?

231
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:47,080
It's Fongnuan.

232
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:49,240
Why can't I hear you?

233
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:50,880
- Shia!
- Shia!

234
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:58,240
Wait, this is a shoe!

235
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:04,720
I'm not sad.

236
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:07,360
I'm not sad either.

237
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,840
Fongnuan!

238
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:11,320
Wrong way!

239
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:17,400
This way! Back to my residence!

240
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:19,560
Let's go!

241
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:22,600
Junior! Fongnuan!

242
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:25,720
- Junior! I said, wrong way!
- Fongnuan!

243
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,920
Junior! Fongnuan!

244
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:35,160
- Fongnuan!
- Junior!

245
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:40,240
Junior, where are you?

246
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:42,440
- Junior!
- Fongnuan!

247
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:44,000
Help!

248
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,440
Fongnuan!

249
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:48,000
Help!

250
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,960
Stop choking me!

251
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:56,080
You've all gotten into trouble again.

252
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:00,800
How did you end up in the water?

253
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:05,120
- We were drunk.
- We were drunk.

254
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:13,040
Who should I punish?

255
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:15,120
Me.

256
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:17,040
I failed to look after them properly.

257
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,200
Next time we get drunk...

258
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,880
We'll make sure
not to fall into the water again.

259
00:21:23,880 --> 00:21:25,680
There won't be a next time.

260
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:27,560
How can you even think of getting drunk again?

261
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:33,320
You may return to your residences.

262
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:34,720
Yes.

263
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,600
Your Highness!

264
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:42,880
If I don't dry you off, you'll fall ill.

265
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:46,120
You could've asked Lha
or one of the other maids to do it.

266
00:22:46,120 --> 00:22:48,720
Lha went to the temple with Maneethip.

267
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:51,320
If I asked the other maids,

268
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:55,280
they'd find out you got drunk
and fell into the water.

269
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:59,480
Then, I'll do it myself.

270
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:04,600
How many times have I told you?

271
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:08,360
It's improper for a lady to drink alcohol.

272
00:23:08,360 --> 00:23:10,880
Prince Fah Haam needed someone to comfort him.

273
00:23:10,880 --> 00:23:11,760
As his companion,

274
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:15,240
I couldn't just sit there and listen
without drinking.

275
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:18,200
- Is it your duty to comfort everyone?
- No, Your Highness.

276
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:20,720
Only those who matter to me.

277
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:26,040
You've become quite sharp-tongued.

278
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:31,400
Are you scolding me for talking back?

279
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:36,760
You should rest.

280
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:42,840
You may stay here tonight.

281
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:44,960
I won't be staying in this room.

282
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:47,360
Your cousin sleeps here alone.

283
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:49,680
Why is that?

284
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:55,480
Maneethip has been going to the temple
to pray every evening.

285
00:23:55,480 --> 00:24:01,680
She should be back soon.
I'll tell her what happened.

286
00:24:06,560 --> 00:24:08,000
Your Highness.

287
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:14,120
Ever since I woke up,

288
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:17,800
I haven't fully regained my memory.

289
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:22,360
I don't know
why my cousin is behaving this way.

290
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:27,320
But I know she's a good person.

291
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:32,720
Please don't be angry with her.

292
00:24:33,760 --> 00:24:35,440
I know that all too well.

293
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:42,640
I understand Maneethip,
and accept her for who she is.

294
00:24:43,840 --> 00:24:46,200
But your cousin...

295
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:48,400
has yet to accept me.

296
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:52,600
You said yourself that she needs time.

297
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,840
So I must give her time.

298
00:25:14,400 --> 00:25:18,320
You want me to send people
to gather information in Wang Nam Lin?

299
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:20,200
What would you like to know, Your Highness?

300
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:23,000
I wish to know everything about Maneethip,

301
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,600
especially her past.

302
00:25:27,960 --> 00:25:30,600
Have your people find out for certain...

303
00:25:31,560 --> 00:25:34,240
whether she ever had a lover in Wang Nam Lin.

304
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:42,640
Isn't it too late, Your Highness?

305
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:47,120
What good would knowing that do?

306
00:25:48,120 --> 00:25:50,720
For this marriage to work,

307
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:54,680
we must get to know each other better.

308
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:58,600
Perhaps I know too little about Maneethip.

309
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:01,760
Or perhaps I never knew her at all.

310
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:06,040
It may be too late.

311
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:09,200
But I'd rather know the truth.

312
00:26:11,120 --> 00:26:13,080
See to it that this is done discreetly,

313
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:15,520
and as soon as possible.

314
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:18,120
I shall.

315
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:34,320
It's getting late.

316
00:26:34,320 --> 00:26:36,240
Why hasn't she returned yet?

317
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:44,000
Excuse me.

318
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:50,040
Do you know which temple Cousin Maneethip
visits for her evening prayers?

319
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:53,680
Princess Maneethip is at Wat Khao Nam Saeng
in the forest, my lady.

320
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:57,560
I see. Which way is the temple?

321
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,320
Cousin.

322
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:09,080
Where are you?

323
00:27:25,760 --> 00:27:27,800
Wat Khao Nam Saeng.

324
00:27:28,760 --> 00:27:30,520
Is this really the place?

325
00:27:37,680 --> 00:27:39,480
Why have you come to see me?

326
00:27:45,200 --> 00:27:49,040
I didn't come to see you.
I should be asking why you followed me.

327
00:27:50,040 --> 00:27:52,560
Do you think you're that important?

328
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:57,840
Why do you keep pointing a knife at me?

329
00:27:57,840 --> 00:28:00,720
I don't like
strangers wandering around my property.

330
00:28:02,760 --> 00:28:04,840
I'll ask you one last time.

331
00:28:04,840 --> 00:28:07,120
Why have you come here?

332
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:09,320
I came to see Cousin Maneethip.

333
00:28:09,320 --> 00:28:11,760
She's here for her evening prayers.

334
00:28:15,120 --> 00:28:16,760
You've come to the wrong temple.

335
00:28:17,800 --> 00:28:22,480
But the maid told me
to go straight, turn left, then right,

336
00:28:22,480 --> 00:28:24,760
until I reached a tamarind tree.
And from there...

337
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:27,560
Your Highness! Which way is Wat Khao Nam Saeng?

338
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:30,320
Wait for me! Your Highness.

339
00:28:31,760 --> 00:28:34,840
Prince Mueang Fah. Wait for me.

340
00:28:39,760 --> 00:28:41,520
You're the only person around here.

341
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:44,520
If you won't tell me,
who else am I supposed to ask?

342
00:28:44,520 --> 00:28:45,880
If you wish to know,

343
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:47,800
come and help me pick some lotuses,

344
00:28:47,800 --> 00:28:50,000
and I'll tell you.

345
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:51,560
Pick lotuses?

346
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:56,080
No. I won't.

347
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:58,160
Go ahead and do it yourself.

348
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:31,440
What are you picking lotuses for?

349
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:33,240
To offer them to the monks.

350
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:40,360
So, where is Wat Khao Nam Saeng?

351
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:45,280
Even if I tell you now, you can't go there yet.

352
00:29:45,280 --> 00:29:47,080
Help me pick the lotuses first.

353
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:50,640
Fine.

354
00:29:57,320 --> 00:30:00,840
The lotuses we offer to the monks
must still be in bud.

355
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:04,840
Their leaves must be intact,
and their stems mustn't be too short.

356
00:30:14,920 --> 00:30:16,840
You'll bruise it if you hold it like that.

357
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:40,320
Am I doing it right?

358
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:45,560
It's not hard once you put your mind to it.

359
00:31:30,120 --> 00:31:32,480
What are you doing at this temple?

360
00:31:33,320 --> 00:31:36,400
If you want to know
where Wat Khao Nam Saeng is,

361
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:38,120
then keep quiet.

362
00:31:38,680 --> 00:31:42,760
If you wanted some peace and quiet,
why did you make me get into this boat?

363
00:31:42,760 --> 00:31:45,080
You always have to talk back.

364
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:48,280
I'm not talking back.
I'm just being reasonable.

365
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:53,200
I didn't even want to get into this boat
in the first place.

366
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:56,280
All I want is to know
where Wat Khao Nam Saeng is.

367
00:31:56,280 --> 00:31:58,640
I need to find my cousin.

368
00:31:58,640 --> 00:32:00,880
I'm worried about her.

369
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:03,680
Why did you make me pick lotuses?

370
00:32:13,600 --> 00:32:15,000
Now you're quiet again.

371
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:32,320
The temple you're looking for
is across that wooden bridge.

372
00:32:33,160 --> 00:32:35,480
Turn left at the large banyan tree.

373
00:32:36,320 --> 00:32:39,160
Then walk another 200 steps,
and you'll be there.

374
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:41,400
Thank you.

375
00:32:51,120 --> 00:32:54,560
I'll come help you pick lotuses again sometime.

376
00:32:54,560 --> 00:32:55,800
No need.

377
00:33:09,640 --> 00:33:12,320
You needn't have gone
to the trouble of looking for me.

378
00:33:13,320 --> 00:33:15,440
I'm quite content here at the temple.

379
00:33:20,960 --> 00:33:25,880
You and Prince Saen Thep... are married.

380
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:29,640
Why not give him a chance...

381
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:32,360
to be by your side?

382
00:33:36,040 --> 00:33:41,280
I want you to have someone you can lean on.

383
00:33:42,680 --> 00:33:45,200
I want you to be happy.

384
00:33:47,840 --> 00:33:49,320
Fongnuan,

385
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:53,000
my happiness...

386
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:54,640
is you.

387
00:33:56,600 --> 00:33:59,160
Just seeing you healthy again...

388
00:33:59,840 --> 00:34:02,400
and able to lecture me like this...

389
00:34:03,080 --> 00:34:05,240
is enough to make me happy.

390
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:11,920
Since you've come all this way to find me,

391
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:18,520
why don't the three of us...
stay here together tonight?

392
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:21,120
Tomorrow,

393
00:34:22,120 --> 00:34:24,520
I'll ask Prince Saen Thep's permission...

394
00:34:25,320 --> 00:34:28,360
for you two to move into our residence.

395
00:34:35,240 --> 00:34:37,520
I don't think that's a good idea.

396
00:34:37,520 --> 00:34:42,360
What if Prince Saen Thep...
wants to spend time with you?

397
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:45,400
That's right.

398
00:34:45,400 --> 00:34:50,400
It would be better for Lady Fongnuan and me
to stay where we are.

399
00:34:58,520 --> 00:35:03,200
We'll come visit you more often.

400
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:05,400
How does that sound?

401
00:35:08,880 --> 00:35:11,280
Even without you two,

402
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:15,760
my maids keep me company every night.

403
00:35:45,680 --> 00:35:47,680
<i>Don't you love me at all?</i>

404
00:35:48,640 --> 00:35:52,240
<i>All this time, I never knew. But now I do.</i>

405
00:35:52,240 --> 00:35:56,080
<i>I cannot accept it. Please, leave me be.</i>

406
00:36:07,920 --> 00:36:10,920
So this is where
you two brothers have been hiding.

407
00:36:18,160 --> 00:36:20,040
Such sorrowful music.

408
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:26,320
And an empty liquor jar.

409
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:27,960
Prince Kong Tai.

410
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:43,200
Prince Kong Tai told me you've been heartsick.

411
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:46,080
It seems he was right.

412
00:36:50,760 --> 00:36:55,120
What Kong Tai knows, all of Wiang Kaew knows.

413
00:36:57,200 --> 00:37:02,120
Even if he hadn't told me, I would have known.

414
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:06,320
A son can never hide anything from his mother.

415
00:37:07,360 --> 00:37:13,040
Though I'm not your birth mother,
I've raised you since you were little.

416
00:37:19,640 --> 00:37:21,800
If I weren't a prince,

417
00:37:25,280 --> 00:37:27,960
if I'd been born your son,

418
00:37:31,200 --> 00:37:33,480
perhaps life would be much easier.

419
00:37:37,160 --> 00:37:38,960
Not necessarily.

420
00:37:39,720 --> 00:37:43,400
It might be a hundred
or even a thousand times harder.

421
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:51,520
As the head of the ladies-in-waiting,
I face difficulties every single day.

422
00:37:53,280 --> 00:37:56,040
How could my son have an easy life?

423
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:11,640
If only I were even half as strong as you,

424
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:14,560
I'd be content.

425
00:38:17,640 --> 00:38:21,560
No amount of drinking will ease
the pain you're going through.

426
00:38:22,640 --> 00:38:26,960
The pain is in your heart.
That's where it must heal.

427
00:38:28,200 --> 00:38:33,320
But this wound runs deep.

428
00:38:35,720 --> 00:38:40,240
Wounds take time to heal.

429
00:38:40,240 --> 00:38:46,040
Once yours has fully healed,
the pain will fade.

430
00:38:48,360 --> 00:38:50,560
Give it time.

431
00:38:50,560 --> 00:38:53,360
Time will heal your wound.

432
00:38:53,960 --> 00:38:59,600
And once you've healed,
don't let yourself get hurt again.

433
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:46,600
The King has issued a royal decree...

434
00:39:48,200 --> 00:39:50,640
appointing Lady Fongnuan...

435
00:39:52,400 --> 00:39:56,160
as a lady-in-waiting in the outer court
of Wiang Kaew,

436
00:39:58,720 --> 00:40:02,040
under the supervision of Lady Homjan,

437
00:40:02,760 --> 00:40:05,240
effective immediately.

438
00:40:22,680 --> 00:40:26,720
The King has spoken.
You must accept the royal decree.

439
00:40:26,720 --> 00:40:29,040
- But I don't want to go to Wiang Kaew.
- You must.

440
00:40:30,200 --> 00:40:32,520
Accept the royal decree at once, Fongnuan.

441
00:40:46,720 --> 00:40:50,000
I humbly accept the royal decree.

442
00:41:19,960 --> 00:41:22,800
Why has Father summoned her to Wiang Kaew?

443
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:26,360
How would I know?

444
00:41:26,360 --> 00:41:28,040
But I think it's for the best.

445
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:31,760
At least she won't be moving in here.

446
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:34,400
She'd only be eating our food
and using up our resources.

447
00:41:35,160 --> 00:41:39,200
- Can't you order her back to Wang Nam Lin?
- No!

448
00:41:39,200 --> 00:41:43,160
- I cannot defy an order from Wiang Kaew.
- I don't want her anywhere near Father.

449
00:41:43,160 --> 00:41:45,920
Nor do I want her getting close
to any of my siblings.

450
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:56,760
But I think...

451
00:41:58,080 --> 00:41:59,880
we should let her go.

452
00:42:00,960 --> 00:42:05,120
So she can keep an eye
on what goes on inside Wiang Kaew...

453
00:42:05,120 --> 00:42:07,000
and report back to us.

454
00:42:12,120 --> 00:42:13,960
But I don't understand.

455
00:42:14,920 --> 00:42:16,480
Why her?

456
00:42:23,240 --> 00:42:27,000
Perhaps she was meant
to serve in the inner court.

457
00:42:28,080 --> 00:42:33,000
Fongnuan was appointed to the outer court,
not the inner court.

458
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:36,680
- The outer court?
- I had someone look into it.

459
00:42:36,680 --> 00:42:40,840
Homjan was the one who asked Father
to summon Fongnuan.

460
00:42:40,840 --> 00:42:42,760
Homjan?

461
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:45,360
Fah Haam and Kong Tai's nursemaid?

462
00:42:46,560 --> 00:42:49,040
Why would she want Fongnuan there?

463
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:52,280
That's what puzzles me.

464
00:42:55,920 --> 00:42:58,320
Normally, ladies-in-waiting at Wiang Kaew

465
00:42:58,320 --> 00:43:02,280
are selected or appointed by the Queen.

466
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:07,080
But this time, Homjan went directly
to Father to request a royal decree.

467
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:10,840
Don't you see?

468
00:43:10,840 --> 00:43:14,400
This interference goes against court customs.

469
00:43:14,400 --> 00:43:18,120
I'm worried that if Fongnuan,

470
00:43:18,120 --> 00:43:23,760
the cousin of Saen Thep's wife,
wins Father's favor,

471
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:28,080
your position as Crown Prince
could be threatened.

472
00:43:28,080 --> 00:43:33,800
If she manages to get close to Father
and learn Wiang Kaew's secrets,

473
00:43:35,560 --> 00:43:39,480
she could gain considerable influence.

474
00:43:42,320 --> 00:43:46,400
Fongnuan could help Saen Thep
gain Father's favor,

475
00:43:47,360 --> 00:43:52,360
or perhaps Homjan will intervene

476
00:43:52,360 --> 00:43:57,640
to help Fah Haam and Kong Tai,
whom Father has never favored,

477
00:43:57,640 --> 00:43:59,720
win his favor instead.

478
00:44:11,200 --> 00:44:14,520
Rumors of your misdeeds

479
00:44:14,520 --> 00:44:18,560
with Prince Pha Wiang are spreading.

480
00:44:21,720 --> 00:44:24,080
Whether they're true or not,

481
00:44:25,240 --> 00:44:27,760
your reputation will suffer either way.

482
00:44:31,720 --> 00:44:37,800
I think you should...
keep a close eye on Fongnuan.

483
00:44:38,720 --> 00:44:40,760
She cannot be trusted.

484
00:44:50,960 --> 00:44:52,920
I'm not going to Wiang Kaew.

485
00:44:52,920 --> 00:44:55,640
I thought you wanted me
to move in here with you.

486
00:44:56,960 --> 00:44:58,960
Fongnuan,

487
00:44:58,960 --> 00:45:03,360
being summoned to Wiang Kaew is a great honor.

488
00:45:03,360 --> 00:45:09,200
The opportunity to serve the King
is a rare privilege.

489
00:45:09,200 --> 00:45:10,840
But I don't want to go.

490
00:45:10,840 --> 00:45:12,760
Why not?

491
00:45:12,760 --> 00:45:14,320
Are you afraid?

492
00:45:17,720 --> 00:45:22,400
Moving to Wiang Kaew isn't what I want.

493
00:45:23,560 --> 00:45:26,520
I know you value your freedom.

494
00:45:27,360 --> 00:45:29,840
You prefer to stick to what you know.

495
00:45:29,840 --> 00:45:31,560
But think about it.

496
00:45:32,240 --> 00:45:34,920
By moving there,

497
00:45:34,920 --> 00:45:37,160
you'll have a chance to learn new things...

498
00:45:37,920 --> 00:45:41,000
and show what you're capable of.

499
00:45:42,200 --> 00:45:43,720
Fongnuan,

500
00:45:44,800 --> 00:45:50,560
venturing beyond what you know
doesn't mean losing who you are.

501
00:45:51,440 --> 00:45:53,480
It means you're growing.

502
00:45:54,600 --> 00:45:55,440
But...

503
00:45:55,440 --> 00:45:58,000
But if you refuse to go to Wiang Kaew,

504
00:45:58,000 --> 00:46:00,000
your cousin and I,

505
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:02,560
perhaps even everyone
at Chiang La-or's Residence,

506
00:46:02,560 --> 00:46:04,320
will suffer the consequences.

507
00:46:04,920 --> 00:46:09,160
If Father becomes angry,
we could all be punished.

508
00:46:09,160 --> 00:46:11,240
Punished?

509
00:46:20,960 --> 00:46:22,600
I promise...

510
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:26,920
I'll look after you, even while we're apart.

511
00:46:26,920 --> 00:46:31,640
Your cousin and I... will visit you often.

512
00:46:31,640 --> 00:46:33,400
You won't be lonely.

513
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:36,560
I don't want to cause trouble for anyone,

514
00:46:37,640 --> 00:46:40,000
especially you and my cousin.

515
00:46:43,320 --> 00:46:45,760
I'll go to Wiang Kaew.

516
00:47:14,200 --> 00:47:17,040
Fongnuan has been summoned to Wiang Kaew?

517
00:47:17,040 --> 00:47:19,480
Where did you hear that, Mother?

518
00:47:19,480 --> 00:47:24,080
I have eyes and ears everywhere in Wiang Kaew.
I know everyone's every move.

519
00:47:24,720 --> 00:47:27,480
You're close to Kong Tai.

520
00:47:27,480 --> 00:47:30,040
And Kong Tai is close to Saen Thep.

521
00:47:32,120 --> 00:47:34,200
Look into this matter.

522
00:47:34,200 --> 00:47:37,200
Find out whether Chiang La-or is behind it.

523
00:47:39,480 --> 00:47:42,760
If you have eyes and ears
everywhere in Wiang Kaew,

524
00:47:43,440 --> 00:47:45,720
why do you need me to investigate?

525
00:47:45,720 --> 00:47:49,280
They can't uncover every detail.

526
00:47:51,440 --> 00:47:54,120
This concerns us both.

527
00:47:54,920 --> 00:47:58,880
If Chiang La-or is plotting to use Fongnuan
to win your father's favor,

528
00:47:59,720 --> 00:48:03,600
I want to be prepared before it's too late.

529
00:48:09,320 --> 00:48:11,600
Do as I say.

530
00:48:11,600 --> 00:48:13,920
Talk to Kong Tai.

531
00:48:13,920 --> 00:48:16,640
He's close to Saen Thep.

532
00:48:16,640 --> 00:48:20,080
- And Saen Thep--
- I prefer to keep things simple.

533
00:48:22,120 --> 00:48:24,360
I have an easier way.

534
00:48:32,640 --> 00:48:36,880
I don't know who's behind this, either.

535
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:41,600
Before I knew it,
I was being sent to Wiang Kaew.

536
00:48:41,600 --> 00:48:43,560
I'm still confused.

537
00:48:44,440 --> 00:48:47,160
Did Royal Consort Chiang La-or order you to go?

538
00:48:47,160 --> 00:48:48,400
No.

539
00:48:48,400 --> 00:48:53,040
That day, she looked
just as surprised as I was.

540
00:48:54,680 --> 00:48:58,840
I really don't want to go.
Who knows what awaits me there?

541
00:49:01,360 --> 00:49:04,440
Junior, don't worry.

542
00:49:04,440 --> 00:49:08,000
I'll look after you in Wiang Kaew.

543
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:10,760
- Really?
- Of course.

544
00:49:12,040 --> 00:49:14,360
I owe you my life.

545
00:49:15,400 --> 00:49:18,120
You saved me.

546
00:49:18,120 --> 00:49:19,520
Remember?

547
00:49:21,720 --> 00:49:23,480
You're my junior.

548
00:49:25,360 --> 00:49:28,800
As your senior,
it's only right that I protect you.

549
00:49:30,960 --> 00:49:32,240
Deal.

550
00:49:57,920 --> 00:49:59,520
So...

551
00:49:59,520 --> 00:50:05,000
you really don't know who's behind this?

552
00:50:06,080 --> 00:50:07,440
No.

553
00:50:17,480 --> 00:50:19,440
It was me, Homjan.

554
00:50:19,440 --> 00:50:22,000
I had you summoned to Wiang Kaew.

555
00:50:22,000 --> 00:50:23,640
Auntie?

556
00:50:25,200 --> 00:50:27,320
You mustn't address her that way.

557
00:50:27,320 --> 00:50:29,640
You must call her Lady Homjan.

558
00:50:30,720 --> 00:50:32,640
Lady Homjan,

559
00:50:33,360 --> 00:50:35,720
I don't know anything about court duties.

560
00:50:35,720 --> 00:50:37,400
I'll teach you.

561
00:50:38,000 --> 00:50:41,400
Come here tomorrow
and I'll teach you your duties.

562
00:50:41,400 --> 00:50:43,280
Tomorrow?

563
00:50:43,280 --> 00:50:44,480
Yes.

564
00:50:52,080 --> 00:50:57,760
You'll be a lady-in-waiting at Wiang Kaew,
not a prisoner.

565
00:50:57,760 --> 00:51:01,480
If you wish to visit your family,
you may ask the King's permission.

566
00:51:03,280 --> 00:51:08,640
For now, I'd like you to keep this a secret.

567
00:51:09,640 --> 00:51:15,120
Outer court ladies-in-waiting
work closely with the King.

568
00:51:15,120 --> 00:51:19,880
The more people know,
the greater the danger to you.

569
00:51:35,720 --> 00:51:38,840
They raided the villagers' rice barns
in Ullavee.

570
00:51:38,840 --> 00:51:42,040
Merng Mang's soldiers cornered
and killed four of them.

571
00:51:42,040 --> 00:51:45,080
The rest escaped with the rice.

572
00:51:47,360 --> 00:51:51,760
I'm truly sorry
we couldn't recover the stolen rice.

573
00:51:51,760 --> 00:51:52,800
It's all right.

574
00:51:52,800 --> 00:51:55,920
Thank you for eliminating those vile bandits.

575
00:51:55,920 --> 00:51:57,680
You and your men have done well.

576
00:52:02,960 --> 00:52:06,320
Would you like an Eight Directions Yantra
like ours?

577
00:52:11,080 --> 00:52:15,960
This yantra protects us in battle.

578
00:52:15,960 --> 00:52:19,800
Every soldier of Merng Mang bears one.

579
00:52:19,800 --> 00:52:23,360
The Eight Directions Yantra
symbolizes our oath...

580
00:52:23,360 --> 00:52:27,280
to lay down our lives
for our nation and our King.

581
00:52:27,280 --> 00:52:29,400
I'm not from Merng Mang.

582
00:52:37,840 --> 00:52:41,640
Why is the Eight Directions Yantra circular?

583
00:52:41,640 --> 00:52:46,760
Merng Mang's Eight Directions Yantra
is tattooed with oil.

584
00:52:46,760 --> 00:52:48,400
It leaves no visible mark.

585
00:52:49,080 --> 00:52:52,760
But the circle in the center
is tattooed in ink...

586
00:52:52,760 --> 00:52:56,360
to remind us that we bear the yantra...

587
00:52:56,960 --> 00:52:59,000
and must abide by its rules.

588
00:53:00,480 --> 00:53:05,000
For if we break them,
the yantra will no longer protect us.

589
00:53:13,360 --> 00:53:15,120
Is something wrong?

590
00:53:17,560 --> 00:53:22,760
I'll order the soldiers
to bring the bandits' bodies back to Ullavee.

591
00:53:22,760 --> 00:53:24,600
What for?

592
00:53:24,600 --> 00:53:29,680
I want to investigate and find out...

593
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:32,880
who was behind this.

594
00:53:36,600 --> 00:53:38,880
They died violent deaths.

595
00:53:38,880 --> 00:53:43,440
They should be cremated here
so their spirits may rest in peace...

596
00:53:43,440 --> 00:53:47,240
rather than linger
and bring misfortune upon the kingdom.

597
00:53:57,440 --> 00:54:00,240
If word of the raid on the rice barns gets out,

598
00:54:01,440 --> 00:54:04,160
it could affect our tribute collection.

599
00:54:07,560 --> 00:54:09,480
I agree with Pha Wiang.

600
00:54:11,400 --> 00:54:14,200
Proceed with the cremation.

601
00:54:33,560 --> 00:54:35,080
Take the bodies away for cremation.

602
00:54:53,440 --> 00:54:56,240
So you've all heard?

603
00:54:56,920 --> 00:54:58,680
So much for keeping it a secret.

604
00:55:00,040 --> 00:55:03,440
There's no such thing as a secret in Ullavee.

605
00:55:04,200 --> 00:55:06,560
Especially in Wiang Kaew.

606
00:55:12,200 --> 00:55:16,680
So, how do you feel
about moving to Wiang Kaew?

607
00:55:18,520 --> 00:55:22,440
So much happens every day, even out here.

608
00:55:22,440 --> 00:55:27,720
Who knows what awaits me once I'm inside?

609
00:55:27,720 --> 00:55:33,000
You're our friend now.
We'll always be there for you.

610
00:55:35,440 --> 00:55:37,080
Come on!

611
00:55:37,080 --> 00:55:38,360
Cheers!

612
00:55:38,360 --> 00:55:40,800
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

613
00:55:44,080 --> 00:55:45,320
Cheers.

614
00:55:49,120 --> 00:55:51,360
Thank you so much.

615
00:55:52,200 --> 00:55:54,880
Ever since I traveled through...

616
00:55:58,440 --> 00:56:02,880
I mean, since I moved to Ullavee.

617
00:56:02,880 --> 00:56:07,640
You, you, and you
are the only true friends I have.

618
00:56:08,240 --> 00:56:13,280
No matter what happens in the future,

619
00:56:13,880 --> 00:56:19,400
I hope we'll always be friends.

620
00:56:20,880 --> 00:56:22,080
Wait.

621
00:56:27,920 --> 00:56:31,960
You're talking strangely.
As if you know the future.

622
00:56:34,200 --> 00:56:38,320
Junior, if you know the future,
you must tell your senior.

623
00:56:38,320 --> 00:56:42,360
When will Mother stop controlling me?

624
00:56:43,560 --> 00:56:46,320
Will I meet the woman of my dreams?

625
00:56:47,440 --> 00:56:50,280
I can't wait to find out who she is.

626
00:56:58,760 --> 00:57:01,320
<i>Phaya Devaraja,</i>

627
00:57:01,320 --> 00:57:06,160
<i>the last king, the most ruthless of all,</i>

628
00:57:06,160 --> 00:57:11,200
<i>who murdered his own siblings
to seize the throne.</i>

629
00:57:12,920 --> 00:57:14,400
Junior.

630
00:57:15,960 --> 00:57:17,400
Junior.

631
00:57:19,360 --> 00:57:21,280
- Fongnuan!
- Yes?

632
00:57:23,720 --> 00:57:25,800
What's wrong?

633
00:57:25,800 --> 00:57:29,000
You're acting strangely again.

634
00:57:29,600 --> 00:57:32,880
I'm thinking about Wiang Kaew.

635
00:57:34,240 --> 00:57:38,600
As for your futures, I don't know.

636
00:57:39,160 --> 00:57:43,600
I don't even know what my own future holds.

637
00:57:46,320 --> 00:57:48,280
By the way,

638
00:57:48,280 --> 00:57:53,480
of all you princes,

639
00:57:53,480 --> 00:57:55,400
were any of you born elsewhere

640
00:57:55,400 --> 00:57:59,880
or brought here from another city?

641
00:58:00,440 --> 00:58:04,480
We were all born in Ullavee.

642
00:58:07,080 --> 00:58:11,760
What about Prince Pha Wiang?

643
00:58:12,680 --> 00:58:14,320
Prince Pha Wiang?

644
00:58:16,960 --> 00:58:17,880
I heard

645
00:58:17,880 --> 00:58:22,360
Prince Pha Wiang is
Prince Indraraja's half-brother.

646
00:58:22,360 --> 00:58:26,680
I suppose he might have lived here.

647
00:58:26,680 --> 00:58:28,480
No.

648
00:58:29,320 --> 00:58:34,000
Though Prince Pha Wiang comes and goes
as if this were his own home,

649
00:58:35,400 --> 00:58:38,920
he isn't considered a native of Ullavee.

650
00:58:42,880 --> 00:58:47,480
Merng Mang is just a small border city.

651
00:58:47,480 --> 00:58:51,600
It could never invade and conquer Ullavee.

652
00:58:52,960 --> 00:58:57,280
I see. Is there anyone else like that?

653
00:59:01,360 --> 00:59:06,840
If you mean someone
with close ties to Merng Mang,

654
00:59:08,520 --> 00:59:10,880
my brother is another.

655
00:59:13,600 --> 00:59:18,520
Mueang Fah was born in Ullavee,

656
00:59:21,520 --> 00:59:24,400
but was sent to Merng Mang as a child.

657
00:59:26,800 --> 00:59:32,760
Prince Mueang Fah was exiled to the border?

658
00:59:44,880 --> 00:59:48,800
<i>Mueang Fah was born in Ullavee,</i>

659
00:59:48,800 --> 00:59:51,640
<i>but was sent to Merng Mang as a child.</i>

660
00:59:51,640 --> 00:59:54,640
<i>Phaya Devaraja...</i>

661
00:59:54,640 --> 00:59:57,560
<i>I strip you of your title
as third in line to the throne.</i>

662
00:59:57,560 --> 00:59:59,840
<i>was the most ruthless of all,</i>

663
00:59:59,840 --> 01:00:05,800
<i>because he seized the throne
by murdering his own siblings.</i>

664
01:00:43,600 --> 01:00:45,720
[Next Week]
<i>All ladies-in-waiting must perform their duties</i>

665
01:00:45,720 --> 01:00:48,200
<i>from dawn until dusk.</i>

666
01:00:48,200 --> 01:00:49,920
<i>Besides attending to the King,</i>

667
01:00:49,920 --> 01:00:52,720
<i>you must familiarize yourself
with his interests,</i>

668
01:00:52,720 --> 01:00:57,400
<i>such as literature, music,
governance, and combat.</i>

669
01:00:57,400 --> 01:01:01,120
<i>I won't mention the rice,
the soldiers' bodies, or the fake bandits.</i>

670
01:01:01,120 --> 01:01:04,240
<i>But you must tell Indraraja
exactly what I instruct you to say.</i>

671
01:01:04,240 --> 01:01:09,800
<i>You still want to know
about Princess Maneethip's past, don't you?</i>

672
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:13,880
<i>I'll determine an auspicious time.</i>

673
01:01:13,880 --> 01:01:17,320
<i>So your return to Wiang Kaew goes smoothly.</i>

674
01:01:17,320 --> 01:01:18,520
<i>Why must it be Mueang Fah?</i>

675
01:01:18,520 --> 01:01:20,600
<i>I never believed in the Hour of the Plunderer.</i>

676
01:01:20,600 --> 01:01:22,320
<i>An auspicious time?</i>

677
01:01:22,320 --> 01:01:24,280
<i>The Hour of the Ruler.</i>
